Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EtherCAT/Pci1203Monitor.cpp: Open() is split on its "reading the IO map" line (same line, no line moves): the second half -- DI/DO max channels, ring status, the DI/DO station maps and their attribution, DiBatchOpen_, opened=true / disabled=false -- is now the body of OpenIoLayout_, unchanged; it sits inside Open()'s #if HAVE_PCI1203, so RescanRing's call is #if-guarded too. RescanRing calls it after re-scanning the slaves and re-opening the axes. Impl gets diPortsReq / doPortsReq (the widths the FIRST Open() asked for, same line); Rescan() and RescanRing re-open with them -- they used the width clamped to what the card reported at the last open, so ports of a module missing then could never come back.

readonly / control gates PASS; Pci1203 tests 6/6; code-after-comment scan 0; OpenIoLayout_ present in the Debug exe. No card in the tests: the IO-map rebuild is compiled, not run. Debug + release (affected targets). WORKLOG section 2 row 146.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
